{{Portrait}}
Rico (formerly Ricochet) is a {{Rarity|Super Rare}} [[Brawler]] with moderately low health but a very fast reload speed and a high burst damage potential. He was one of the 15 Brawlers who released at the first Beta launch. Both his attack and Super fire long-ranged bullets that can bounce off walls and continue traveling. However, his Super travels further and pierces, dealing damage to multiple enemies at once, though the bullets can only hit the target once. If used correctly, Rico can defeat enemies around walls without coming under enemy fire. His first Gadget, Multiball Launcher, deploys a vending machine that provides cover for him and his teammates, and blasts waves of bouncy bullets all around it upon being destroyed. His second Gadget, Multiball, fires a large bullet that splits into 3 smaller bullets upon hitting a wall or enemy Brawlers. His first Star Power, Super Bouncy, grants extra damage to his bullets from his attack or Super if they bounce. His second Star Power, Robo Retreat, increases his movement speed when he is at low health. His Hypercharge, Trick Shot King, allows the projectiles from his Super to bounce much further than normal.

==Attack: Bouncy Bullets==
{{Quote|Rico's bullets bounce off walls, gaining range. They can hit enemies behind cover.}}Rico fires a burst of five long-ranged bullets with a slight spread that can bounce off walls, and they each gain 1.67 tiles of additional range for every bounce. This attack has a moderate cooldown, and it takes 0.6 seconds to complete.

==Super: Trick Shot==
{{Quote|Rico fires a long burst of bullets that pierce through enemies and bounce off walls, gaining range.}}Rico's Super fires a larger, longer-ranged burst of twelve piercing bullets with a slight spread that can bounce off walls, and they each gain 1.67 tiles of additional range for every bounce. Even though the bullets can pierce through enemies, they can only damage enemies once. This Super has a long cooldown and takes 1.25 seconds to complete. However, he can't attack or reload while using his Super, and it is cancelled if Rico is knocked back, pulled, or stunned. 

==Gadgets==
===Multiball Launcher===
{{Quote|Rico deploys a vending machine with 4000 health. Rico can bounce attacks off the vending machine until it explodes, firing bouncing projectiles in all directions. Cooldown: 22 seconds.}}{{Gadget|1}}
Rico deploys a vending machine that has 66.67% of his health. It blocks non-piercing or bouncing/splitting narrow enemy fire, and Rico can bounce his attack and Super off it. If the vending machine is destroyed, it blasts a wave of piercing bullets with a range of 11.67 tiles all around himself that each deal 133.33% the damage as one of his attack bullets. These bullets behave identically to his Super's bullets, but last for a shorter period. Even though the bullets can hit multiple enemies, they can only damage each enemy once. If Rico places down another vending machine, the initial one will be destroyed and will blast a wave of piercing bullets.

{{Quote|When Rico bounces bullets off the vending machine, extra bullets are added to it when it explodes.}}{{Buffie|Gadget}}
With the Buffie, if Rico bounces bullets off the vending machine, more bullets will be added to it when it explodes.

===Multiball===
{{Quote|Rico fires a big bullet that splits into 3 smaller bullets when hitting a wall or enemy Brawlers. Cooldown: 17 seconds.}}{{Gadget|2}}Rico fires a big bullet that splits into 3 smaller bullets upon hitting a wall or enemy Brawlers. Both the big and small bullets deal damage equal to 300% of the damage of one of Rico's bullets, and the small bullets can also bounce off walls. Even though the smaller bullets can't pierce through enemies, they can stack its damage dealt to the enemy by behind the enemy by hitting them multiple bullets at once. This Gadget doesn't use ammo. 

{{Quote|Bullets also slow enemies.}}{{Buffie|Gadget}}
With the Buffie, both the big and small projectiles slow enemies hit by 20% for 1.5 seconds.

==Star Powers==
===Super Bouncy===
{{Quote|Rico's bullets, from attack and Super alike, get supercharged by their first bounce and deal +240 damage!}}{{StarPower|1}}
If Rico's bullets (from either his main attack or his Super) bounce off a wall, they will glow and deal 240 additional damage at Power 11, increasing his main attack bullets' damage by 40% and his Super bullets' damage by 33.33%. The bullets can only be supercharged once, and enemies will take regular damage if the bullets aren't bounced before they hit enemies. 

{{Quote|Bounced bullets also give 10% Super charge on hit.}}{{Buffie|Star}}
With the Buffie, the bounced bullets also charge the Super by 10% more.

===Robo Retreat===
{{Quote|Rico runs 25% faster when his health falls below 40%.}}{{StarPower|2}}
When Rico's health falls below 40%, he runs 25% faster, allowing him to move much faster than most Brawlers and escape enemies more easily. This speed boost disappears when his health restores above 40%.

{{Quote|Increase movement speed by up to 40% when Rico is at 10% health.}}{{Buffie|Star}}
With the Buffie, Rico's movement speed boost increases as his health decreases, reaching up to 40% at 10% health.

==Hypercharge: Trick Shot King==
{{Quote|Rico's Super's projectiles bounce even further!}}{{Hypercharge}}
When activated, projectiles from Rico's Super bounce much further than usual, gaining 6 tiles of additional range for the first 8 bounces, instead of 6. He also gains a 20% speed boost, as well as a 5% damage and shield boost.

{{Quote|Rico's Main Attack has increased bullet speed and fires additional bullets.}}{{Buffie|Hyper}}
With the Buffie, Rico's attack has 7 bullets and a faster projectile speed. Increased Hypercharge duration by 2 seconds.

==Mutation==
{{RemovedContent|section}}
{{Quote|All Rico's projectiles bounce more.}}<div style="float:right">[[File:Mutation.png|64px|link=]]</div>Rico's projectiles from his attack, Super, and Multiball Launcher Gadget bounced more, and therefore stayed on the map longer. The healing from his Bouncy Castle Gadget was also decreased by 50%.

==Wasabi Power==
{{RemovedContent|section}}
{{Quote|More bullet bounces? More bullet bounces.}}<div style="float:right">[[File:Inferno Wasabi.png|64px|link=]]</div>Rico's projectiles could only gain additional range for the first 5 bounces instead of 6, but they gained 6.67 tiles from each bounce, for a total attack range of 43 tiles. This did not affect his Super's projectiles.

==Tips==
===Game Modes and Maps===
*Rico is an exceptional asset for Special Events. In these scenarios, he delivers sustained fire on robots thanks to his impressive damage output and rapid reload speed, all while remaining safe by attacking from behind cover. His Robo Retreat Star Power proves invaluable for evading danger, whether it’s while waiting for teammates to respawn or evading the Boss and its attacks. Additionally, his piercing and high-damaging Super enables him to inflict substantial damage on robots, further enhancing his effectiveness on the battlefield.
*Because Rico can bounce his shots off walls, which increases each bullet's range for every bounce, he's outstanding on enclosed maps such as [[Cavern Churn]] and [[Pinball Dreams]], where other sharpshooters would have difficulty hitting shots due to the abundance of walls.

===Recommended Build===
*Rico's Multiball Launcher Gadget deals very high damage if all of the bullets hit. However, it's very inconsistent as the bullets spread out from the launcher, so it's best to use this Gadget at point-blank range so all of the bullets can hit a target. However, this Gadget is mainly used in an enclosed area where the bullets will bounce multiple times and guarantee a hit to an enemy trapped in the area.
*Rico and [[Meeple]] can be used as a deadly trap if used correctly. Rico fills up his vending machine all the way and waits for his Gadget to come off, cooldown, and then when an enemy comes, Meeple throws down Mansions of Meeple and Rico throws down a new Gadget and destroys his old one, instantly doing damage and possibly killing an enemy (this requires having a Gadget Buffie for Rico).
*Rico's Multiball Launcher does require a enemy to destroy it, however if you have waited enough and the enemy has not destroyed it, you can place down another Gadget and manually destroy the old Gadget 
*Rico's Super Bouncy Star Power grants his bullets an extra 256 damage upon bouncing. While it doesn't seem like much additional damage for each bullet, when all five bullets are bounced, an additional 1280 damage is added, making his total damage 4480. Similarly, a bounced Super will deal a total of 11712 damage. This encourages Rico to bounce shots off walls for them to deal more damage (especially in maps like [[Snaked Assault]] and [[Turnaround]]) where he has the potential to bounce his shots from a safe distance. However, don't shoot Rico's Super directly onto a target and expect the bullets to deal damage to the target again when they bounce off another wall, as his Super's bullets only deal damage once, and to properly use this Star Power, you must bounce the Super off a wall in such a way that the bounced shots hit the target and not the normal shots.
*Rico's Robo Retreat Star Power allows Rico to perform guerrilla tactics by rushing into fights and then escaping when you're on low health. Doing so allows more of your bullets to hit enemies due to the increased accuracy. If you're a good sniper, you should back away from fights and attack from a distance. If you're a good dodger, you can keep firing to prevent Rico from healing and stay below 40% health to use the speed buff to dodge enemy fire and even outrun fast Brawlers like assassins, tanks, and [[Max]].

===Strategies===
===Other===
*When shooting off of a wall at a fleeing enemy, move towards the place you're shooting to increase the range of your bullets so that you can hit more of them. If they're hiding in bushes, move side-to-side while shooting off of the wall to cover more ground with your bullets.
*Similarly to [[Colt]], though difficult to perform, Rico can chain his Super if every bullet from his Super successfully hits an enemy Brawler. This is more practical if Rico hits several enemies in a single Super.

